From 4c160f7b60477de0b3d78a8021aa0cfd8fb55a9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:02:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45: Settlers cost one citizen, not two

A city had to reach size 3 before it could finish Settlers, so the
second city came around turn 21 (median of 12 AIs on 5 seeds). With one
citizen a size 2 city can finish them: median turn 16.5, and about 45%
more cities by turn 40. Issue 350.
---
 data/civ45/units.ruleset | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/civ45/units.ruleset b/data/civ45/units.ruleset
index 7e1fda3..975ee4c 100644
--- a/data/civ45/units.ruleset
+++ b/data/civ45/units.ruleset
@@ -519,7 +519,9 @@ sound_move_alt = "m_generic"
 sound_fight   = "f_settlers"
 sound_fight_alt = "f_generic"
 build_cost    = 30
-pop_cost      = 2
+; Freeciv45: one citizen, not two, so a size 2 city can finish Settlers
+; (John's play test, issue 350: the second city came too late).
+pop_cost      = 1
 attack        = 0
 defense       = 1
 hitpoints     = 20
@@ -549,8 +551,8 @@ means of founding new cities.\
 Settlers found cities (or join one) and do nothing else: roads, \
 irrigation, mines and forts are the Workers' job.\
 "), _("\
-TIP: optimal production of Settlers occurs in cities of at most \
-size 4, or cities with a Granary of at most size 6.\
+Building Settlers takes one citizen from the city, so the city \
+must be at least size 2.\
 ")
 
 [unit_migrants]
-- 
